{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792923603,"nonce":"to0UBr2116jYj/D0IC+azFyODUw=","title":"LSP: the editor extension","message":"Part of 1626b90d930d209e848220743e00494408af449d2cdabdddea70f6c0a5337545 (caribou lsp).\n\nA VS Code extension activates in a workspace that has a .cbproj. It does\nfour things:\n- starts `caribou lsp` for the project's Haxe, Wren, Lua, Python and\n  frontend files;\n- points the Python server at .caribou/stubs (pyright's stubPath);\n- points lua-language-server at .caribou/lua (workspace.library);\n- turns off the Haxe and Wren servers for those workspaces, since\n  caribou-lsp serves both.\n\nIt finds the caribou command on the path or in the project's toolchain.\nWrenLift's extension (wren_lift/editors/vscode-wrenlift) is the model for\npackaging.","files":null}]}